      <h1>Lithium Price &amp; Supply</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Market Intelligence · Data period 2022–2025 (varies by figure) · Last reviewed 2026-09-15</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> Lithium carbonate is the dominant lithium product — about <strong>52% of the
        global lithium market in 2025</strong>, with battery-grade material the largest sub-segment. The price story is
        extreme volatility: lithium chemical export prices peaked around <strong>USD 48,000 per ton in 2023</strong>,
        then fell roughly <strong>62% to about USD 18,000 per ton in 2024</strong>, before a supply-tightening rebound
        in 2025.
      </div>
      <h2>Market snapshot</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Geography</th><td>China</td></tr>
